<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3374" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbŏrārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		arbor (a technical form of arboreus), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to trees</i>, <i>tree-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falx,</span>”
				i. e. <i>for pruning trees</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 10, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">31, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 22, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">picus,</span>”
				<i>a woodpecker</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 16, 53, § 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proventus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 11</span></i>
			 and 23.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbŏrārĭa</span></b>  (sc. herba),
				ae, f., <i>the
			blackivy</i>, as growing on trees, <i><span class="en">App.
				Herb. 98</span></i>.</div>
